[[Cookbook:Edikang Ikong|Edikang Ikong]] Soup is a Nigerian most popular delicacy that is prepared using [[Cookbook:Pumpkin|Pumpkin]] Leaf and Water leaf. It is highly nutritional and very easy to prepare. Edikang Ikong translates as Cooked [[Cookbook:Vegetable|Vegetable]] Soup in English language. It is native to the Efik and Ibibio people of southern Nigeria.

== Recipe ==

* [[Cookbook:Pumpkin|Pumpkin Leaf]] (Desired Quantity)
* Water Leaf
* [[Cookbook:Onion|Onions]]
* Stock fish (medium size)
* Roasted or dried Fish
* Cray Fish 
* Fresh Cow skin (Kpomo)
* Goat Meat (preferred)
* Half a Bottle of [[Cookbook:Palm Oil|Palm oil]]
* Salt
* Pepper
* Seasoning cubes
* unshelled Periwinkle

== Preparation ==

# Add a half spoon of salt to water and Wash your meat and cow skin thoroughly.
# After washing put into a clean pot, add a pinch of salt, pepper and seasoning cube and onions to taste and place on fire. When it boils, add the unshelled periwinkle, washed dried fish and Stock fish and a half cup of water, cook it till it is done and set aside.
# While stock is on fire, wash your pumpkin leaf and waterleaf and onions dice them separately.
# Sieve water from your prepared stock and keep aside.
# Place the stock on fire, add Palm oil, either half or a full bottle, add crayfish, pepper, salt, seasoning cubes (2knorr depending on the size of soup), stir well to incorporate everything till it boils.
# Add the waterleaf, stir it add onions and pumpkin leaf, stir and cover the pot to cook for 2 minutes
# Enjoy with any swallow of your choice.



